  "summary": "A centrifugal pump and its sealed electric motor form one unit that sits on the floor of a sewage wet well, fully submerged. Raw sewage enters through the bottom inlet into a two-channel non-clog impeller whose wide passages pass solids and fibres. Two mechanical seals with an oil chamber between them keep water out of the motor. The pump slides down two guide rails and couples automatically to the duckfoot bend on the floor, so it can be lifted out for service without entering the well.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Rotodynamic (centrifugal), radial flow",
    "configuration": "Submersible, close-coupled, vertical, guide-rail installed"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "impeller": "Closed two-channel non-clog (vortex and cutter impellers are alternatives)",
    "free_passage_note": "Free passage (largest sphere passed) is a key selection value — check data sheet.",
    "seals": "Tandem mechanical seals with oil barrier and moisture sensor (typical)",
    "installation": "Guide rails + duckfoot auto-coupling"
  },
